From: Thorsten Blum <blum@kernel.org>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 12:52:30 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] init: use kmalloc() in do_initcalls()

Use kmalloc() since strscpy() already NUL-terminates command_line.

Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20261114115230.30345-4-blum@kernel.org
Signed-off-by: Thorsten Blum <blum@kernel.org>
Signed-off-by: Andrew Morton <akpm@linux-foundation.org>
Cc: Masami Hiramatsu <mhiramat@kernel.org>
Cc: Breno Leitao <leitao@debian.org>
Cc: Sang-Heon Jeon <ekffu200098@gmail.com>
Cc: Christian Brauner <brauner@kernel.org>
Cc: Wilson Felipe Pereira <wfelipe@google.com>
Cc: Ryan Roberts <ryan.roberts@arm.com>

 init/main.c |    2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)
---
 init/main.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/init/main.c b/init/main.c
index 3068821309d7f..30f2d11b7370e 100644
--- a/init/main.c
+++ b/init/main.c
@@ -1487,7 +1487,7 @@ static void __init do_initcalls(void)
 	size_t len = saved_command_line_len + 1;
 	char *command_line;
 
-	command_line = kzalloc(len, GFP_KERNEL);
+	command_line = kmalloc(len, GFP_KERNEL);
 	if (!command_line)
 		panic("%s: Failed to allocate %zu bytes\n", __func__, len);
 
-- 
2.47.3

